> Additional Useful Terminal Functions

### Process Management

ps: lists running processes. `ps aux` shows all processes for all users.
kill <PID>: terminates a process by ID. `kill 1234`
killall <name>: terminates by name. `killall firefox`
top or btop: interactive system resource monitor.

### Archiving and Compression

tar -cvf archive.tar <files>: creates tar archive.
tar -xvf archive.tar: extracts tar archive.
gzip <file>: compresses file (adds .gz).
gunzip <file.gz>: decompresses.

### Networking

ping <host>: checks connectivity.
curl <URL>: downloads or interacts with a URL.
wget <URL>: downloads a file.
ssh <user>@<host>: connects to remote machine.

### System Information

uname -a: kernel version and architecture.
df -h: disk space in human-readable format.
free -h: RAM and swap usage.
uptime: system uptime and load averages.

### Terminal Shortcuts

ctrl+C: interrupt current command.
ctrl+Z: suspend current command (background).
ctrl+D: exit shell or send EOF.
ctrl+R: search command history.
!!: repeat last command. `sudo !!` repeats last with sudo.
tab: auto-complete.

### Aliases

add shortcuts in ~/.zshrc and run `source ~/.zshrc` to apply.

default SNAPS-OS aliases:
find - fzf-based file finder with previews
microfind - like find, opens selected in micro
ls - eza with icons, colors, grouping
la - list all files
ll - long format
lt - tree format, 4 levels deep
l. - hidden files only
update - sudo pacman -Syu
jctl - minimal journalctl command
cmdhist - search and select from command history
tipme - get a random tip
cowtip - get a random tip from an RGB cow

### fzf Integration

type `**` and press <tab> in the terminal for fzf autocomplete on file paths.

### Environment Variables

printenv: display all environment variables.
echo $VARIABLE: print a specific variable's value.
export VARIABLE=value: set a variable for the current session.

### `locate`

locate <pattern>: quickly find files using a pre-built database.
run `sudo updatedb` first if the database is not current.
